From: beitlab Robotics MilkV duo OS <image/patches>
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] duos: identify boot volumes supporting Wi-Fi provisioning

Local change to the pinned SDK's device/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd/genimage.cfg.
Keep the SDK partition layout, fip.bin and boot.sd (from rawimages/). Include a
non-secret capability marker from the rootfs overlay so the PC helper can
reject old images that lack the first-boot importer.
---
diff --git a/device/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd/genimage.cfg b/device/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd/genimage.cfg
--- a/device/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd/genimage.cfg
+++ b/device/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-sd/genimage.cfg
@@ -5,5 +5,14 @@ image boot.vfat {
 			"fip.bin",
 			"rawimages/boot.sd",
 		}
+		file playground/wifi-supported {
+			image = "fs/boot/playground/wifi-supported"
+		}
+		file playground/setup-supported {
+			image = "fs/boot/playground/setup-supported"
+		}
+		file playground/user-supported {
+			image = "fs/boot/playground/user-supported"
+		}
 	}
 	size = 128M
